  "description": "A large open medical and life-science AI agent skill library for the OpenClaw / NanoClaw framework — ~869 SKILL.md modules across clinical, genomics, drug-discovery, bioinformatics, omics, and data-science categories. The clinical set (~119 skills) covers areas such as clinical reports, decision support, prior authorisation, FHIR development, and HIPAA compliance; the majority is research/bioinformatics tooling (variant calling, single-cell, genomics databases). Skills are read directly by a model-agnostic agent and require a user-supplied LLM/API key. Note: the README shows an MIT badge but the repository contains no LICENSE file, so the licence is unverified. The clinical skills are not described as independently validated, and this is agent tooling, not a cleared medical device.",
